.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt BOBCTL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm bobctl
.Nd free the GPU from the assistant's model for a game, or load it back
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Cm status | on | off | toggle
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The assistant's model holds about 8 GB of video memory while it is
loaded, most of a 10 GB card.
.Nm
unloads it, or loads it back, through Ollama's API; an idle Ollama holds
almost none.
It needs no root.
With a desktop notification service it also says what it did there.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm status
The default: whether the model is loaded, and the free video memory.
.It Cm off , Cm disable , Cm game
Unload every loaded model.
.It Cm on , Cm enable
Load the model, by asking it for one token; up to five minutes.
.It Cm toggle
Whichever of the two it is not.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev OLLAMA_HOST
Default
.Ql http://localhost:11434 .
.It Ev BOB_MODEL
Default
.Ql bob .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when done; 1 when Ollama is not installed or the model would not load,
usually for want of memory.
.Sh EXAMPLES
On a kldload desktop on 2026-09-30, with this release's
.Nm
first on the path:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ bobctl status
Bob: unloaded (GPU free for gaming) | VRAM free: 8839 MiB
# (exited 0)
.Ed
